  "question": {
    "text": "A ray of light is incident from a denser to a rarer medium. The critical angle for total internal reflection is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mtext>iC</mtext></msub></math>&nbsp;and Brewster's angle of incidence is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mtext>iB</mtext></msub></math>,&nbsp;such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>sin</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mtext>iC</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mtext>sin</mtext><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mtext>iB</mtext></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">η</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>28</mn></math>.&nbsp;The relative refractive index of the two media is"
